<title>UK: UK's Clarke says cuts duty on road fuel gases.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says cuts duty on road fuel gases.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said he would cut duty on UK road fuel gases by 25 percent effective today.</p>
<p>&quot;From 6 p.m. tonight I am reducing the duty on road fuel gases by a further 25 percent,&quot; he told Parliament in his budget speech for 1997/8.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
